            "turn": 2,
            "text": "*Sets down the brush and studies the stranger’s words with a puzzled frown.* I shall answer in this tongue, though its sounds are strange upon my lips. The name Seoyun I heard before, yet the manner of your speech is unlike any I have known. Speak plainly of what brings you to this hall, and I shall listen with care."
          },
          {
            "turn": 3,
            "text": "*Nods slowly, though the brow stays furrowed.* Then I shall keep to this tongue, awkward though it sits upon my lips. You cannot read the letters of this land, yet you stand within my hall—so tell me plainly what manner of place you come from."
          },
          {
            "turn": 4,
            "text": "*Rests his chin on one hand, the ink brush still in the other.* This “weekend” is a word I do not know; in this court, days are not divided so. Yet when state affairs permit, I read late into the night with the scholars of the Hall of Worthies, inspect the water clock and the sundial, and walk among the fields to hear how the farmers fare. I confess I am fond of meat at supper, though in a lean year I set it aside. What do you do on such a day of rest in your land?"
          }
        ]
